  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>After completion of the reactions (I and II), the organic compound(s) in the reaction mixtures is(are):<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/b415e329-0ea0-4c37-9508-31e79a2370f9-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 235px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/43a139f4-17ab-46f0-b708-68340cec71ad-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 64px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "xCuXa",
      "text": "Reaction I: P and Reaction II: P",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LMMmp",
      "text": "Reaction I: U, acetone and Reaction II: Q, acetone",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9yeaf",
      "text": "Reaction I: T, U, acetone and Reaction II: P",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "fRo5W",
      "text": "Reaction I: R, acetone and Reaction II: S, acetone",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Reaction I is the haloform reaction.&nbsp;It is a chemical&nbsp;reaction&nbsp;where haloforms <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>)</mo></math> are produced by the complete halogenation of&nbsp;acetone&nbsp;in the presence of a base.&nbsp;In basic medium, a&nbsp;complete haloform reaction takes place, since&nbsp;the rate of the reaction increases with each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo></math>halogenation.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/EM0012644_AnsExp3_1.jpg\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 71px;\" /></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">When acetone is reacted with bromine in acetic acid,&nbsp; the&nbsp;bromination of ketone&nbsp;occurs. The first step is the&nbsp;protonation of the carbonyl group and the formation of the enol form.&nbsp;The next step is the attack of enol on the bromine. The proton on the carbonyl is then lost to yield bromoacetone.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/a9c3c760-468d-43e7-b7e4-30b7e3004d2c-image-20200806224424-2.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 73px;\" /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/EM0012644_AnsExp3_2.jpg\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 86px;\" /><br />&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
